t 2 is equal  to 5 to the power of z  but there are no integer solutions to  this equation so we cannot have y is  equal to 0.  we are left with the case that y is  equal to 1.  if we substitute y is equal to 1 we get  1 plus 4 is equal to 5 to the power of z  this has an obvious solution that z is  equal to 1.  so this gives the solution x is equal to  zero  and y and z are both equal to one  so we've solved this case we have one  more case to solve which is x is less  than zero let's work on this  if x is less than zero what would happen  if y were greater than or equal to zero  in that case z would have to be greater  than zero  in this equation let's subtract four to  the power of y from both sides by the  given assumptions 5 to the power of z  and 4 to the power of y are both  integers  so their difference will be an integer  but since x is less than 0 the left hand  side is not an integer  this is a contradiction in other words  there are no integer solutions for the  stated conditions  y cannot be greater than or equal to  zero we must have that y is less than  zero  if x and y are both less than zero  then the sum of three to the x plus four  to the y  will be less than or equal to one over  three plus one over four which is less  than one  this implies that z is less than zero  so x y and z are all less than zero  let's let a be negative x b be negative  y and c be negative z so that a b and c  are positive so our equation then  becomes the following  let's multiply both sides of the  equation by 3 to the power of a  multiplied by 4 to the power of b  multiplied by 5 to the power of c  we can then simplify this equation and  we get the following result  now 5 is a factor on the left hand side  but 5 is not a factor on the right hand  side  this is a contradiction  therefore there are no integer solutions  for these conditions  thus we've solved the problem  we can see that if x is less than 0  there are no integer solutions if x is  greater than 0 there's exactly one  solution that x is equal to y is equal  to z is equal to two and if x is equal  to zero there's exactly one solution  that x is equal to zero and y and z are  both equal to one  so there are exactly two solutions to  this equation in integers x y and z  wow  thanks for making us one of the best  communities on youtube see you next  episode of mind your decisions where we  solve the world's problems one video at  a time  [Music]

